From 5b7b896790c3602a9610629d04a2c52e4f614f78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 11:04:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] python3: reject control characters in POP3 commands
 (CVE-2025-15367)

poplib.POP3._putcmd did not reject C0/C1 control characters in commands,
allowing CR/LF (and other control-char) injection into the POP3 protocol
stream. Guard the command line with a control-character regex and raise
ValueError, matching the upstream fix.

Source-only backport: the upstream commit's test and Misc/NEWS.d entry are
omitted (Lib/test is not shipped in the image; the release note is not
applicable to a patch).

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/b234a2b67539f787e191d2ef19a7cbdce32874e7]
Signed-off-by: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
---
 Lib/poplib.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Lib/poplib.py b/Lib/poplib.py
index 4469bff..b97274c 100644
--- a/Lib/poplib.py
+++ b/Lib/poplib.py
@@ -122,6 +122,8 @@ class POP3:
     def _putcmd(self, line):
         if self._debugging: print('*cmd*', repr(line))
         line = bytes(line, self.encoding)
+        if re.search(b'[\x00-\x1F\x7F]', line):
+            raise ValueError('Control characters not allowed in commands')
         self._putline(line)
 
 
